# Design System and Shadcn UI

## Absolute Rule

NEVER use native HTML elements (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<table>`, etc.) if an equivalent Shadcn component exists. The interface must be 100% consistent.

## Available Shadcn Components in the Project

If you need any of these interfaces, use the corresponding Shadcn component. If it is not yet installed in the project, generate the code assuming it will be (importing from `@/components/ui/`):

- **Forms & Inputs:** Form (react-hook-form + zod), Button, Input, InputOTP, Textarea, Checkbox, RadioGroup, Select, Switch, Slider, Label, Toggle, ToggleGroup.
- **Navigation & Menus:** NavigationMenu, Menubar, Breadcrumb, DropdownMenu, ContextMenu, Tabs, Pagination.
- **Modals & Overlays:** Dialog, AlertDialog, Sheet (Sidebar/Drawer), Drawer, Popover, HoverCard, Tooltip.
- **Data Display:** Table, Card, Carousel, Chart (Recharts), Calendar, Avatar, Badge, Accordion, Collapsible, ScrollArea, Separator, AspectRatio.
- **Feedback:** Alert, Skeleton, Progress, Sonner (Toasts).

## UI Best Practices

- For forms, ALWAYS use the combined Shadcn `Form` structure with `zod` for validation.
- Use Tailwind CSS for all additional styling via the `className` prop and the Shadcn `cn()` utility function.
- Maintain consistency with the CSS variables (primary colors, radius) defined in `globals.css`.
